  {
   "id": 131,
   "type": "text",
   "title": "Live vs Statistics copy — and the ops-subscription limitation",
   "gridPos": {
    "h": 11,
    "w": 24,
    "x": 0,
    "y": 30
   },
   "options": {
    "mode": "markdown",
    "code": {
     "language": "plaintext",
     "showLineNumbers": false,
     "showMiniMap": false
    },
    "content": "### Live store vs statistics copy\n\n| Source | Count | Notes |\n|---|---|---|\n| `operation-plan-wrapper` (live, core-es7) | **41** | authoritative, via `_count` |\n| `utm-op-statistics` (statistics copy) | **37** | feeds the Drone Plan Dashboard |\n\nThe difference is **4 documents**. This is a small lag, **not** evidence of a broken pipeline. Do not raise an incident on this gap alone — corroborate with ingest errors in `utm-statistics-service` before concluding anything.\n\nNote the live store has a genuine lifecycle spread (PROPOSED / AUTHORIZED / ACTIVATED / CLOSED) whereas the statistics copy is entirely CLOSED — they capture different stages, so a count difference is expected by design.\n\n---\n\n### `ops-subscription` — NOT TIME-FILTERABLE\n\nConfirmed via `_field_caps`: every field (`state`, `subscriptionType`, `providerId`, `dataFormat`) is mapped as **`text`** and reports **`aggregatable: false`**. The index also has **no date field**.\n\nGrafana's Elasticsearch datasource always applies a time filter and requires aggregatable fields for terms panels, so no live subscription panel can be built. Validated count at build time: **8 documents**.\n\n**To fix:** add `keyword` sub-fields and a timestamp to the `ops-subscription` mapping."
   },
   "pluginVersion": "12.1.1",
   "transparent": false
  },
